# Text files are checked out with LF endings on EVERY platform, including
# Windows.
#
# This is not cosmetic. With `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows clone materialises
# CRLF, and a CRLF checkout made `tests/changelog-notes.test.ts` fail with a bare
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token` on the import of the shebang'd
# `scripts/changelog-notes.mjs` — while the same commit passed everywhere else.
# The file parses under plain Node either way; it is vitest's transform that
# rejects it, so the error pointed at the import line and named no file.
#
# Git only normalises what it detects as text, so binary assets are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf
